# Personal financial data and secrets - never commit these.
# This project is designed to be cloned with none of this present;
# skills/portfolio/references/BOOTSTRAP.md rebuilds it all from a
# user-provided transactions.csv on first run.
#
# These paths are the DEFAULT data location (<repo>/data/). If PORTFOLIO_DATA_DIR
# points somewhere else, the data lives outside the repo entirely and none of
# this applies - see mcp_servers/portfolio_tools/paths.py.
mcp_servers/portfolio_tools/.env
data/personal/

# The split is mechanical, with no per-file exceptions: everything under
# data/personal/ is ignored, everything under data/impersonal/ is committed.
# The line is ownership, not subject matter - data/impersonal/ (ticker_map.csv,
# company_overrides.csv, price_history/, news/) is factual data about securities
# that is identical for everyone, so it's shared and ever-growing: resolving a
# ticker or fetching a day's close is work nobody should repeat. What you hold
# and what it's worth lives in data/personal/. Don't add impersonal paths here,
# and don't put anything position-specific there.

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# portfolio MCP server's venv (needs Python >=3.10) - reproducible via
# `pip install -r mcp_servers/portfolio_tools/requirements.txt`, see bootstrap.sh
mcp_servers/portfolio_tools/.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/

# Server runtime state - process metadata, not source or data
data/.pipeline.lock
mcp_servers/portfolio_tools/.server.pid
mcp_servers/portfolio_tools/.server.log
